&lt;p&gt;The server listens on &lt;code&gt;GRPC_ADDR&lt;/code&gt; and advertises &lt;code&gt;GRPC_ENDPOINT&lt;/code&gt; in the
enrollment response. The bearer travels in the metadata,
&lt;code&gt;authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;token&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, and is verified as for the HTTP API. &lt;code&gt;Watch&lt;/code&gt;
sends the current set at once, then a new one each time the tenant&amp;rsquo;s routes
change, for the tenant &lt;strong&gt;the device enrolled into&lt;/strong&gt;, found by &lt;code&gt;public_key&lt;/code&gt;,
which must be enrolled by the caller (&lt;code&gt;NOT_FOUND&lt;/code&gt; otherwise,
&lt;code&gt;PERMISSION_DENIED&lt;/code&gt; once the person has left that tenant).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The server serves it over TLS with &lt;code&gt;TLS_CERT&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;TLS_KEY&lt;/code&gt;. The clients
(&lt;code&gt;pkg/routeclient&lt;/code&gt;) speak TLS to it, checked against the system&amp;rsquo;s roots,
except to a loopback address, and refuse a plaintext one.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>